## 5. Configuration — `config.json`

```json
{
  "qwen_base_url": "http://<local-llm-host>:<port>/v1",
  "qwen_model": "auto",
  "memory_dirs": [
    "/path/to/workspace/memory"
  ],
  "memory_files": [
    "/path/to/workspace/MEMORY.md"
  ],
  "db_path": "/path/to/scripts/memory/data/memory.db",
  "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5",
  "chunk_size": 300,
  "top_k_fts": 20,
  "top_k_vector": 20,
  "top_k_final": 5,
  "rerank_with_qwen": false,
  "extract_entities": true,
  "ttl_days": 90
}
```

**Key fields:**

| Field | Notes |
|---|---|
| `qwen_base_url` | Base URL of the OpenAI-compatible API. Do NOT include `/chat/completions`. |
| `qwen_model` | `"auto"` queries `/v1/models` and uses the first result. Set explicitly if needed. |
| `memory_dirs` | Directories to walk for `*.md` and `*.txt` files. Recursive is NOT used — flat only. |
| `memory_files` | Individual files to index (in addition to `memory_dirs`). Glob patterns supported. |
| `embedding_model` | fastembed model identifier. `BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5` gives 384-dimensional vectors at ~50ms/query on CPU. |
| `chunk_size` | Target words per chunk. Chunks follow heading boundaries first, then split by word count. |
| `top_k_fts` | Candidate count from FTS5 search before merge. |
| `top_k_vector` | Candidate count from FAISS search before merge. |
| `top_k_final` | Final results returned. |
| `rerank_with_qwen` | Default `false`. When `true`, top merged candidates are sent to Qwen for semantic reranking. Adds ~2s latency. |
| `extract_entities` | Controls whether `indexer.py` runs entity extraction (can be overridden per-run with `--no-entities` / `--extract-entities`). |
| `ttl_days` | Daily log files older than this are removed from the index (raw files are NOT deleted). |

