## 15. Known Limitations & Future Upgrade Path

| Limitation | Mitigation | Upgrade path |
|---|---|---|
| Scale ceiling ~500K chunks | Corpus unlikely to reach this for months | Swap FAISS flat → FAISS IVF; SQLite embeddings → Qdrant |
| No concurrent write safety | Single writer (indexer runs sequentially) | Add write lock or migrate to Qdrant for concurrent agents |
| Entity extraction quality depends on LLM | Larger/better model = better graph | Model upgrade is transparent (auto-detected) |
| Graph queries are sequential (vector then graph) | Acceptable at current scale | Migrate to Kùzu for single-pass hybrid queries at >100K nodes |
| FTS5 is English-optimised | Corpus is English | Add language-specific tokeniser if needed |

